# 0080-redesign-library-build-settings-sheet.patch -- the owner's approved redesign (prototype target/agent-work/design/project/Main.dc.html, 2026-11-21): a 3D cover flow and a grid in the
# Library with the cloud games in it, state-driven buttons (the get-task-allow rule), an anchored touch-and-hold menu, the Build tab's card, the Settings tiles, the new game sheet, the capsule
# tab bar, the warm dark palette; and NO AUTORUN: a build ends on Ready, Play is the only way a game starts.
# Applies after 0079. UNTESTED ON DEVICE AND IN THE SIMULATOR: compiled, and its pure part ran in a host harness (below). Nothing here was looked at on a screen.
#
# NEW FILES
#   * GameAppRedesign.cs (no UIKit; the harness compiles it as it is): LibraryActions (the buttons by state: a game only in a cloud source -> Download, Cancel while it downloads; on this
#     iPhone not built -> Build; built -> Play + Export IPA; built with a certificate that has no get-task-allow -> Export IPA alone + the line "This certificate has no get-task-allow: a game
#     cannot run inside iBuilder. Export it and install it as its own app."; a build running -> Watch the build; paused -> Resume; while a build or a boot runs only Watch / Cancel stay on),
#     LibraryStatus (pill, status and meta words: "In iCloud", "On the NAS", "Not built", "Ready", "Update available", "Downloading 37 %"), LibraryMerge (the games of this iPhone, then the
#     cloud-only base games of Cloud.CloudOnlyGames that no local game stands for by name or base title id, each title once, minus the hidden ones), HoldMenuLayout (the menu anchored to its
#     card: below it, above it for the last row of the grid or when it does not fit below, the left column's at the card's left edge, the right column's ending at its right edge, centred under
#     a carousel cover, never off the screen), HoldMenuPlan (the menu follows the state like the buttons: Download / Cancel the download / Build / Play (development certificate only), Export IPA,
#     Settings, Choose a cover… (not for a cloud-only game), Update, 0076's Pause / Resume the shader preparation and "Prepare the shaders now", 0065's "Cancel the paused build…", the queue,
#     the uploads, Remove download, then Delete… or, for a cloud-only game, Hide from the library), CoverHue (the dominant hue of a cover: a 36-bucket histogram weighted by saturation x value,
#     circular mean in the winning bucket; -1 for a grey cover -> the fixed amber), NoAutorun (below), ProvisionText (the app's own embedded.mobileprovision: expiry, name, get-task-allow;
#     "6 days left", "Development · SideStore · can play here" / "Distribution · … · export only"), DeviceTiles ("On · 6.5 GB" from the increased-memory-limit entitlement and the
#     os_proc_available_memory ceiling at launch; the largest address-space hole "64 GB" against the game table's mem_reserve, "In one hole · <game> needs 16.5"), BuildCardText (the
#     design's stage names, "Shaders 15,383 of 42,848 · 36 %", the note), SheetOptions (which per-game rows the sheet shows as segmented controls, and the settings page's own SetValue rule
#     for a choice made there), HiddenGames, CancelFlags + CancelWriteStream (Cancel of a download).
#   * GameAppRedesignUi.cs (UIKit): Look (the tokens surface #19191f, raised #25252b, line white 8 %; cards 16, pills), FlowCell + CoverFlowView (the 3D carousel), HoldOverlay (the touch-and-hold
#     layer), the Library (BuildLibrary / RefreshLibrary / GridCard / HoldEntries), StyleTabs (the capsule tab bar), the Settings tiles, the Build tab's card, the sheet's launch line.
#
# WHAT CHANGES IN THE APP (every action is an existing one: PrimaryTapped, DownloadSelected, ConfirmExport, ShowCoverChooser, ConfirmDelete, ResumePaused, AskCancel, ToggleWarmPause,
# PrepareNow, AddToBuildQueue, UploadTo, RemoveGameDownload, ShowMods, ShowSaves, ShareGameLogs, SettingsFor, SaveSettings / SaveSettingValues, ImportMenu, BuildStopButtons, ...)
#   * Theme (GameAppTheme.cs): ground #0e0e12, ink #f1ece3, muted ink white 62 % / 55 %, accent #efb15a with black on it, good #6fc782, bad #ec6b66 (the exported player takes them too);
#     AmbientView: a radial glow centred at 50 % / 32 % tinted by a hue (SetHue; SetTint maps a colour to its hue).
#   * Library (GameAppShelf.cs BuildShelf / RefreshShelf -> GameAppRedesignUi.cs): the header ("Library", "4 games · 32.7 GB · 56 GB free", a round grid/carousel toggle kept in
#     NSUserDefaults "library_view": "grid" or the cover flow; an old "list" opens the flow), the prerequisite banners and the killed-build banner as before, then:
#       - the cover flow: 230 pt covers (radius 38), the focused one scaled 1.08, its neighbours 210 pt aside, scaled 0.82, rotated 26° about the vertical axis with a 900 pt perspective, at
#         55 %; a horizontal pan moves the covers with the finger and settles on one (a spring); a tap on a side cover focuses it, on the focused one opens the game's sheet, a touch and hold on it
#         opens its menu; then the title, the meta line, page dots, the round Settings button (the game's sheet) and the state's buttons (54 pt), and the get-task-allow line. The covers are
#         updated in place at every redraw (a redraw every second during a download does not reset a swipe). The ground's glow takes the focused cover's dominant hue.
#       - the grid: two equal columns 14 pt apart inside the 20 pt margins; a card = cover (110 pt), the name on one line with an ellipsis, the status, a progress bar while it downloads or
#         builds, 0070/0076's shader strip, and its actions on ONE row: the primary a pill filling the width, a second action (Export IPA beside Play) a 36 pt round icon-only button (a plain
#         "arrow.up", label "Export IPA"); 36 pt drawings take a 44 pt touch (HitButton). "Touch and hold a game for its actions". The page scrolls vertically only.
#       - touch and hold (0.5 s) on a card: a copy of the card lifts where it is (1.03, the raised ground, a brighter edge), the screen dims (black 45 %, a tap closes; VoiceOver: escape), the
#         compact menu opens anchored to it (HoldMenuLayout, 232 pt, 44 pt rows, Delete in red). It is a layer over the screen, never inside the scroll view. The same entries are the card's
#         VoiceOver custom actions. It replaces the UIContextMenuInteraction of 0062-0076 (whose items are all in it).
#       - cloud games in the library: the cached listing the app already keeps (cloudFiles, listed off the main thread at launch, "launch: cloud listing starts at ..."; nothing new is
#         listed), greyed cover (CIColorControls saturation 0, cached per image) with a cloud mark at the top right, status "In iCloud" / "On the NAS" / "In <provider>", Download as their
#         action (DownloadSelected: the Cloud page's path, which since 0079 also gives the cover on landing), Cancel while it downloads, Hide from the library in their menu (NSUserDefaults
#         "library_hidden"; Settings › Sources › "Hidden from the library" shows them again; a hidden game that lands on this iPhone is forgotten).
#       - an empty library: one card, "Add a game" (the Build tab). The exported apps stay under the library.
#   * Cancel of a download (GameAppLibrary.cs Download, GameAppNas.cs Nas.Download): a Files-folder copy stops in its progress callback (it runs in the copy loop: GameImport.Place removes the .part,
#     the old file stays); the NAS stops in its output stream (CancelWriteStream: the progress of SSH.NET runs on its own thread, where a throw would end the app); a cancelled download is no
#     failure (no alert), starts no build ("Download and build"), logs "download cancelled: <name>". A file iOS itself is still downloading from iCloud before the copy stops only when it reaches
#     the app.
#   * Build tab (GameAppShelf.cs BuildBuildTab): "Build" with the refresh and the accent + (a menu: "Add a game file", "Add from a folder without copying" with the prototype's notes, and "From
#     NAS or Cloud" = the Cloud page); "Now building": a card with the game's cover, its name, the line ("Shaders 15,383 of 42,848 · 36 % · 6 min", "Pausing… (finishes the current shader)",
#     "Paused · 14,990 of 21,990 shaders"), a pill (Building / Pausing… / Cancelling… / Paused / Starting), the five stages with a dot (✓ done, • now) and their times, the bar, Pause / Resume
#     and Cancel (0065's buttons and handlers), "Watch the build", the note (BuildCardText.Note: what really happens to the file with 0073's Optimize storage, and "It ends on Ready: Play starts
#     the game."); "Nothing is building…" when idle; the queue in a card; then as before the shader preparation (0076), the filter and the games of this iPhone and of the cloud (Build, Rebuild,
#     Update, Update & DLC, Download and build) in cards.
#   * Settings (GameAppShelf.cs BuildSettingsShelf): four tiles (Keys "Imported" / "Missing"; Certificate: time left and type, "Missing" with the .p12 to import; Extended memory; Extended
#     address with the focused or built game's need), the storage card ("Storage", "56 GB free of 235 GB", 0064's bar), BUILD (0062-0076's switches: Parallel shader preparation, Low
#     performance, Shader preparation cores, Optimize storage, Clear the shader cache), SOURCES (each source -> the Cloud page, "Add a source", "Hidden from the library"), DIAGNOSTICS ("This
#     iPhone" -> the Keys page with play inside iBuilder / memory / addressing / keys / certificate, Logs, Share the logs, Hidden diagnostics, Build), the footer line. The tiles open the Keys
#     page (or the importers); no row or page of before is gone.
#   * Game sheet (GameAppShelf.cs ShowGameSheet): the cover as a 200 pt header (Close, "Choose a cover…", the name, "id · kind · size"), the primary action (the game's light accent, black words)
#     and Delete (0064's ConfirmDelete with its sizes), the launch line while Play starts the game (the save's copy, then the chain's boot stages, until the game window is up; the sheet stays
#     unless Play first asks something: a hot phone, a reopen after a build), three tiles (Shaders, Saves, Build: FolderSizes and a worker count; the app records no play time, so the
#     prototype's "Play time" is not shown), "Settings for this game" as segmented controls (the launcher rows that are basic, visible, a toggle or 2-3 short choices, at most four; without a
#     launcher the page's Mode / Frame rate / Picture), saved through SaveSettingValues / SaveSettings, and "All settings for this game" (the existing page, pushed), Mods, Saves, Export as its
#     own app, Logs, then MORE (Update and DLC, Update, Show in Files, Cancel the paused build…, Add to the build queue, Remove download, Rebuild from scratch…), SHADERS (0076) and STORAGE.
#   * Tab bar (GameAppLibrary.cs BuildTabBar / ShowTab): 20 pt from the sides, rgba(25,25,31,.86) over the blur; the lit tab an ink capsule with its icon and label, the others an icon with
#     their label for VoiceOver.
#
# NO AUTORUN AFTER A BUILD (the owner). Every path that could start a game without a tap, and what it does now:
#   * the config key boot_after_build: GameAppMain.ConfigText wrote "boot_after_build=" + GAMEAPP_BOOT_AFTER_BUILD (default 0); with 1 the chain booted the game at the end of a build
#     (crates/ibuilder-pipeline boot.rs boot_after_build) or, short of memory, wrote an ARMED Documents/gameapp.boot-only that the next launch started by itself. Now the line is always
#     NoAutorun.ConfigLine = "boot_after_build=0" (the environment variable is no longer read): the chain logs "stage 5 not started: the game is built and signed; it starts when you tap Play"
#     and clears its running marker. The Rust side is unchanged (its default is already 0).
#   * the shim's IBUILDER_FLAG_BOOT_IN_PROCESS (app/gameapp_shim_rust.c): unchanged and needed: it says WHERE stage 5 runs (in this process) when there is one to run: a Play (a boot-only
#     launch, gameapp.boot-only present) or a build with boot_after_build=1, which the app no longer writes.
#   * gameapp.boot-only at launch (GameAppMain.cs): an ARMED request is started only when a Play wrote it (NoAutorun.AtLaunch: the words of "Close and play", Play right after a build in this
#     process, and of "GameApp starts again", a Play after a run in this process); any other armed request (the chain's own after a build, a Play whose process died before the boot) is
#     WITHDRAWN with the log line "gameapp.boot-only withdrawn: it was not written by Play — a build ends on Ready and the game starts only when you tap Play"; an ATTEMPTED one is left (as before).
#   * the build screen: its main button said "Play when it is done" while a build ran (a tap only closed the screen, but the words promised a start): it says "Close"; its steps no longer end with
#     "Launch" (NoAutorun.BuildRows), and neither do the Build tab's. Finish() starts nothing (checked).
#   * kept: Play (PrimaryTapped -> a boot-only run), "Close and play" and "GameApp starts again" (a Play carried out by the next launch), gameapp.args "boot-only" (the harness's own request:
#     the app never writes it), gameapp.continue (the rest of a BUILD after the stage-3 restart: it ends on Ready like any build).
#
# VERIFIED (2026-11-21, M1 Pro)
#   * scripts/check-patches-apply.sh: every patch applies in order, no fuzz, no offset; the repository's patches give exactly the compiled tree (diff -r).
#   * Compile (the device project of build-app.sh step 3, as 0079 did, the two new files added, native references left out): `dotnet build gameapp.csproj -c Release -r ios-arm64 -t:Compile`:
#     the 0079 tree 0 errors / 40 warnings; with this patch 0 errors / 40 warnings, the same per file and code. The UI texts below are in the compiled GameApp.dll (UTF-16); "Play when it is
#     done" is not.
#   * Host harness (target/agent-work/redesign/harness: net11.0, the REAL GameAppRedesign.cs, GameAppUi.cs, GameAppCloud.cs, GameAppImport.cs, ...; the UIKit files' text for the wiring; the
#     Rust boot.rs and the Ocarina game table read from the repository): 118 of 118 checks (the action table for every state with and without get-task-allow; the merge on realistic lists with
#     updates, two sources, a case difference, ids, hidden games; the menu's place for both columns, the last row, one row, no room below or above, the carousel, 20,000 random cases never off
#     the screen; the menu's entries per state; the hue of solid, grey, mixed and wrap-around pictures; the no-autorun rules and their wiring; the provisioning parse and the tile words; the
#     16.5 GiB of the Ocarina table; the inline settings and the preset rule; Cancel: the NAS stream and a REAL GameImport.Place copy stopped by the progress callback leaving the old file and no
#     .part; the owner's grid corrections in the UIKit text). 43 of 43 mutations of the sources are killed (harness/mutate.py, mutations.txt).
#
# NOT VERIFIED
#   * Nothing ran on an iPhone or in the simulator: the look, the cover flow's motion and hit areas (taps use the covers' unprojected places), the 3D transform's look, the hold menu's lift
#     (a snapshot of the card), the blur, the sheet's height, the launch line's timing, VoiceOver, the colours' contrast on the device. APPROXIMATED: the carousel's easing is a 0.45 s spring, not
#     the prototype's cubic-bezier; the glow is HSB from the hue, not oklch; the installer's name is read from the profile's Name / TeamName (else "SideStore or AltStore" when the bundle has
#     ALTBundleIdentifier), not known for every installer; "Play time" has no data in the app.
#   * A NAS download cancelled mid-file: SSH.NET's DownloadFile is assumed to propagate the stream's exception (it writes on the calling thread); the Files-folder copy's stop is tested with the
#     real copy loop, not through a File Provider.
#
# NEW UI STRINGS (worth a marker in app/verify_ipa.sh): "This certificate has no get-task-allow: a game cannot run inside iBuilder. Export it and install it as its own app.",
#   "No cover in this game", "Touch and hold a game for its actions", "Grid or carousel", "Settings of this game", "Close the menu", "Cancel the download", "Hide from the library",
#   "Hidden from the library", "Show the hidden games again?", "Export as its own app", "Settings for this game", "All settings for this game", "Now building",
#   "Nothing is building. + adds a game; its Build button starts it. A build ends on Ready: Play starts the game.", "It ends on Ready: Play starts the game.", "From NAS or Cloud",
#   "Your sources in Settings", "Pick a folder, choose its games", "Your own games and keys only. Nothing is included and nothing is sent anywhere.", "What iOS lets a game use",
#   "Extended memory", "Extended address", "In one hole", "Copying the save before the launch", "Update (build again with the update or DLC)", "Add a source", "Keys, certificate, memory",
#   "Less than a day left", "Type not known", "ready to export", "Assemble and sign", "Translate shaders", "Starting…"; log lines "download cancelled: ",
#   "gameapp.boot-only withdrawn: it was not written by Play", "library: ", and the config line "boot_after_build=0". REMOVED: "Play when it is done".
